    "readout_text": "To evaluate the expression:\n\n$$\n2^3 - 1^3 + 4^3 - 3^3 + 6^3 - 5^3 + \\dots + 18^3 - 17^3\n$$\n\nwe observe that the terms are grouped in pairs of the form:\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 - (2n - 1)^3\n$$\n\nfor $ n = 1 $ to $ 9 $, since the last pair is $ 18^3 - 17^3 $, and $ 2n = 18 \\Rightarrow n = 9 $.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: General Form of Each Pair\n\nWe compute the general form of each pair:\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 - (2n - 1)^3\n$$\n\nExpanding both cubes:\n\n- $ (2n)^3 = 8n^3 $\n- $ (2n - 1)^3 = 8n^3 - 12n^2 + 6n - 1 $\n\nSubtracting:\n\n$$\n(2n)^3 - (2n - 1)^3 = 8n^3 - (8n^3 - 12n^2 + 6n - 1) = 12n^2 - 6n + 1\n$$\n\nSo the entire expression becomes:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^{9} (12n^2 - 6n + 1)\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Break the Sum into Parts\n\nWe can split the sum into three separate sums:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^{9} (12n^2 - 6n + 1) = 12\\sum_{n=1}^{9} n^2 - 6\\sum_{n=1}^{9} n + \\sum_{n=1}^{9} 1\n$$\n\nNow, apply standard summation formulas:\n\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{k} n = \\frac{k(k+1)}{2} $\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{k} n^2 = \\frac{k(k+1)(2k+1)}{6} $\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{k} 1 = k $\n\nFor $ k = 9 $:\n\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10}{2} = 45 $\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{9} n^2 = \\frac{9 \\cdot 10 \\cdot 19}{6} = \\frac{1710}{6} = 285 $\n- $ \\sum_{n=1}^{9} 1 = 9 $\n\nNow substitute into the expression:\n\n$$\n12 \\cdot 285 - 6 \\cdot 45 + 9\n$$\n\nCompute each term:\n\n- $ 12 \\cdot 285 = 3420 $\n- $ 6 \\cdot 45 = 270 $\n- $ 3420 - 270 = 3150 $\n- $ 3150 + 9 = 3159 $\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{3159}\n$$",
